nexI-sec17.2-software-lifecycle", "artifact_type": "regulatory citation", "relevance_note": "Emphasizes the need for a robust software development lifecycle and risk management."}, {"artifact_id": "qmsr-820.10-c-design-development", "artifact_type": "regulatory citation", "relevance_note": "Design controls apply to devices automated with computer software."}], "missing_evidence": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment."], "rationale": "The incident narrative describes a non-recurrent atrial fibrillation-adjacent irregularity detected during ambulatory monitoring, with no adverse patient outcome. While the event was self-resolving and handled at a monitoring/investigation level, recurrence risk is being tracked. This indicates a potential deviation from intended performance that warrants investigation to understand the root cause and prevent future occurrences. The device incorporates software (EU MDR Annex I, Section 17.1), requiring adherence to principles of development lifecycle, risk management, and verification/validation (EU MDR Annex I, Section 17.2).  The incident may trigger obligations under EU MDR Annex I, Section 17.1 regarding repeatability, reliability, and performance. The device is automated with computer software, triggering design control requirements (qmsr-820.10-c-design-development).", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 2}, "final_report_sha256": "114e7607bc289fb700ade723e7a58da654920357cc857a4934ee461b5aef161a", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 0, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence", "deny:technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence"], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0015", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 0, "run_id": "inloop_SYN-IND-0015_1503e90b", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0015", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity":